{
  "title": "Aamal of the 21st Night of Ramadhan",
  "data": "In addition to the common rites of the Qadr Nights, it is recommended to recite the following supplication on this night:\nيَا مُوْلِجَ اللَّيْلِ فِي النَّهَارِ وَ مُوْلِجَ النَّهَارِ فِي اللَّيْلِ\nYAA MOOLIJAL LAYLI FIN NAHAARI WA MOOLIDJAN NAHAARI FIL LAYL\nO Merger of the night into the day and Merger of the day into the night!\nوَ مُخْرِجَ الْحَيِّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَ مُخْرِجَ الْمَيِّتِ مِنَ الْحَيِّ\nWA MUKHRIJAL HAYYI MINAL MAYYITI WA MUKHRIJAL MAYYITI MINAL HAYY\nO Extractor of the living from the dead and Extractor of the dead from the living!\nيَا رَازِقَ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ يَاۤ اَللّٰهُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ\nYAA RAAZIQA MAY YASHAAA'U BI-GHAYRI HISAAB, YAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEM\nO Provider of sustenance to whomsoever You will without measure! O Allah! O All-beneficent! O All-merciful!",
  "merits": "The 21st Night of Ramadan is the second of the Qadr Nights and the night of the martyrdom of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.)."
}
